      "hints": [
        "Use electric field strength as force per unit charge to determine the charge in coulombs.",
        "Then divide the charge by the elementary charge to express it in units of e."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Electric field strength is E = F / Q, so Q = F / E.",
        "The nuclear charge is Q = (6.7 × 10⁻¹⁵) / (1.4 × 10⁴) = 4.8 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.",
        "Since one elementary charge is 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C, the charge is (4.8 × 10⁻¹⁹) / (1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 3.0 e.",
        "The charge on the nucleus is 3.0 e."
      ],
